# Documentation Maintenance

When code changes affect observable behavior, update docs in the **same change**.

| Doc | Update when… |
|---|---|
| `bonuscard_odoo/README.rst` | Feature added, changed, or completed |
| `README.md` | Roadmap status or dev/CI instructions change |
| `bonuscard_odoo/static/description/index.html` | User-visible features change |
| `docs/bonuscard_pos_integration_explanation.md` | POS patch added/renamed/removed; API service or partner method changes |
| `docs/bonuscard_pos_integration_diagram.mmd` | Trigger points or data-flow between POS and backend change |

Checks before finishing:

1. POS method patched/renamed → update explanation.md and diagram.
2. New validation trigger → add to step 3 in explanation.md and diagram.
3. New cancel path → add to step 5 in explanation.md.
4. Roadmap item done → mark Done in README.md.
5. Never describe implemented flows as "(Foundation)" or "Ready for".

When updating AI agent guidance, edit `.github/copilot-instructions.md` first, then
sync `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/` if the condensed rules need the same change.
